# Local source of truth

- Make all code changes in the files of the workspace the user has open (the local project on disk).
- Do not treat a Cloud Agent VM, a detached worktree, or an un-checked-out PR branch as the user's local source.
- If this session cannot see the user's local project files, say so and stop. Ask the user to continue in a local Cursor Agent chat (not Cloud Agent) in that folder.
- After edits, the user should be able to save, run, and debug without fetching another git branch first.
